# Packages this tool needs on the machine it runs on.
#
# Not to be confused with live.list and installed.list, which describe the
# systems this project *builds*. This one describes the machine doing the
# building — a CI runner, or a container on one.
#
# It is a declaration, not an installer: `ubuntu-uki-iso` checks these with
# dpkg-query and stops with a message naming what is missing. It never installs
# anything, because it runs on machines it does not own and because changing
# them would change every other job that shares them.
#
# build/Dockerfile installs a superset of this list, and a test asserts that it
# still does — the image is one way to satisfy the declaration, not the
# declaration itself.

# --- group: build ----------------------------------------------------------
# Everything needed to produce the artifacts: the kernel, the two rootfs
# images, the UKIs and the ISO.

# --- kernel build ----------------------------------------------------------
# The standard dep set, plus dwarves for pahole (CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO_BTF stays
# on) and debhelper/fakeroot/dpkg-dev/devscripts/equivs for `make bindeb-pkg`,
# which shells out to scripts/package/mkdebian.
build-essential
bc
bison
flex
libssl-dev
libelf-dev
libncurses-dev
dwarves
debhelper
fakeroot
dpkg-dev
devscripts
equivs

# --- fetching the source ---------------------------------------------------
git
wget
curl
ca-certificates
gnupg
ubuntu-keyring

# --- image build -----------------------------------------------------------
# mmdebstrap bootstraps both rootfs images; xorriso makes the hybrid ISO;
# mtools and dosfstools build the FAT EFI image without a loop device or a
# mount. sbsigntool is kept because a future Secure Boot story would need it.
mmdebstrap
xorriso
squashfs-tools
mtools
dosfstools
sbsigntool

# --- the UKIs --------------------------------------------------------------
# dracut builds the initramfs, ukify assembles the UKI, and systemd-boot-efi
# provides /usr/lib/systemd/boot/efi/linuxx64.efi.stub — the PE stub the UKI is
# built around, without installing a bootloader.
dracut
systemd-ukify
systemd-boot-efi

# --- packing and unpacking ------------------------------------------------
# dpkg-deb extracts the kernel package's files and builds the UKI package. It
# is used to read archives, never to install them.
dpkg-dev
zstd
xz-utils
bzip2
cpio
kmod
rsync

# --- runtime ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Every step in this project is a Python module, so the interpreter is the
# runtime rather than a transitive detail.
python3

# --- group: test -----------------------------------------------------------
# Only needed to run the QEMU suite. Kept separate because a machine building a
# kernel should not be told it is missing QEMU.
qemu-system-x86
ovmf
expect
